.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-oath-accounts-uri 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-oath\-accounts\-uri \- Add a new account from an otpauth:// URI (prompted when omitted)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-oath\-accounts\-uri\fR [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-touch\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-password\fR] [\fB\-\-remember\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIURI\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a new account from an otpauth:// URI (prompted when omitted).
.PP
HOTP counter specifies the next code\*(Aqs counter. CanoKey cannot start at counter zero; such URIs are rejected. Query parameter names and values accept percent\-encoding; repeated recognized parameters are rejected before connecting to the key.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-touch\fR
Require touch on the CanoKey to generate a code
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Skip the existing\-account check
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-password\fR \fI<PASSWORD>\fR
The password to unlock the OATH application
.TP
\fB\-\-remember\fR
Remember the password on this machine (long\-only: the global \-r/\-\-reader owns the short flag)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIURI\fR]
The otpauth:// URI
